{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PARITY SWEEP (Step 7) — complete. Swept every unscoped-HEAD / head_sha / rev-parse HEAD currency read for the same 'gate-ref anchor vs working-tree HEAD basis mismatch' defect:\n\nFIXED (this work): (1) attest._unscoped_head_drift [plan-review, #2399 core + #2401 shared helper]; (2) drift_floor code_drifted [plan-review Pass-3 finding-drop, #2401].\n\nCORRECT-by-design, NOT parity defects: (3) transition_close.py:401 completion drift guard — the COMPLETION gate pins its default target to HEAD via _pin_completion_ref (ref is None -> resolve_ref('HEAD')), so its verified_at_sha basis IS the working-tree HEAD, matching the close-time head_sha(working) read. Same-basis comparison; no foreign read. This is the KEY asymmetry: plan-review's default gate ref is origin/main (gate-ref basis), completion's is HEAD (working-tree basis). (4) _opcert_signing.py:372/407 — the signing/anchor-SETTING side (records the anchor), correct by design. (5) relation_snapshot.tracker_head_sha — reads the TRACKER (tickets branch) HEAD, a different domain (not code gate-ref currency).\n\nSIBLING 505d-b2c5 ('Claim gate fails OPEN when the current gate ref cannot be resolved: _hash_basis silently substitutes the working tree') — confirmed DISTINCT and left untouched (in_progress under another session): it fails OPEN (substitutes working tree) in a different function (_hash_basis); 1137 fails CLOSED with a foreign value. Not merged, per the non-goal. Note: my shared helper current_head_sha fails CLOSED (raises SnapshotError) on an unresolvable attested gate ref — orthogonal to and non-conflicting with 505d's _hash_basis surface."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788051762452679001,"uuid":"d6098e93-9e39-4b94-823b-9e2239b59a6c"}